README for the Gemini DHS package
=================================

This directory contains the sources for the Gemini DHS (Data Handling
System).

Building
--------

This package requires the following external packages:

 dhsClient (same version as this package)

 DRAMA (1.4.2)
	[ftp://ftp.aao.gov.au/pub/drama/]

 CFITSIO (2.430)
   	[http://heasarc.gsfc.nasa.gov/docs/software/fitsio/fitsio.html]

 SYBASE
 	[http://www.sybase.com/]
  
 EPICS (3.14.4)
 	[http://www.epics.org/] 

 Skycat (2.7.3)
 	[ftp://ftp.eso.org/pub/archive/skycat/README.html]

 Tcl/Tk-8.4.1 and extensions (also required to build skycat)
	[ftp://ftp.eso.org/pub/archive/skycat/README.html]

The configure script searches for these packages by first checking the
environment variables: $DRAMA, $CFITSIO, $SYBASE and $EPICS,
SKYCAT_INSTALL, TCLTK_ROOT, and then using a default location if those
variables are not set.

Once all the required packages are in place, you can configure and
make DHS as follows:

    configure
    make
    make install

This will create a subdirectory of this directory called "release"
that contains the installed libraries, include files and test
programs.



Temporary Note on IMP bug fix (Oct 14, 2002)
=============================================

If using drama-1.4.2/imp-1.6.1, you need to apply this fix
to drama-v1.4.2/drama_source/imp/accconnect.c:

Replace line (124):
    AccMessage.Task = *TaskID;

with:
   AccMessage.Task.Machine = TaskID->Machine;
   AccMessage.Task.Pid = htonl(TaskID->Pid);

Newer versions of IMP should already contain this fix.

